nd et quoi à travers tous les\nprojets, ni la mémoire de projet `Memory1/**/<Nom>1.md`, qui porte ce que le projet SAIT. C'est la\ntrace de ce que Matthieu a demandé, là où le travail se fait.\n\n## Exemple vivant\n\n`ZenRayHoudini/GTA6_Stilt_House/FEEDBACK_tmp.md` et `ZenRayHoudini/ModelingJapan_01/FEEDBACK.md` :\nordre des composants, règles de modélisation isolée, pièges payés (les objets Houdini se comparent\npar leur nom et non par identité, un point Cd écrase un Cd de primitive après une fusion).\n\n## 2 October 2026 : Canonical project feedback and strict append\n\n- This section supersedes the earlier section-insertion instructions: the writer only opens with O_APPEND, locks the file, writes at its end and fsyncs; no existing byte changes. (2 October 2026)\n- `feedback-stack` is the sole implementation; `feedback` remains a compatibility alias that calls the same writer. (2 October 2026)\n- Resolve project IDs and local folders through ZenRayProgress `scripts/AssetsConfig.json` and `~/Library/Application Support/ZenRayAssets/Projects.json`; the canonical file is `~/.claude/Memory1/Projects/<project-id>/FEEDBACK.md`. (2 October 2026)\n- Use `feedback.py add <project-id> <text> --event-id <stable-event-id>` for idempotent capture; corrections append a new dated entry referencing the earlier one. (2 October 2026)\n- Preserve historical feedback in place; `feedback.py link-legacy <project-id> <absolute-source-path>` appends reciprocal references and the original byte hash instead of moving or rewriting it. (2 October 2026)\n- The local Assets service captures human prompts and final iterations from Codex and Claude transcripts when a project matches the working folder unambiguously or its session has an explicit project binding. Ambiguous sessions are never assigned by guesswork. (2 October 2026)\n- Read the canonical file and its linked historical sources on resumption; local TMP, Houdini and Unreal feedback all route to the same project ID. (2 October 2026)\n-